## Conclusion

Our study identified that the regional morphometric variations of children with SeLECTS were nested within the normal variation. The normative modeling offers new opportunities to explore the correlation between individual heterogeneity and clinical manifestations, which may potentially enhance the predictive power of neuroimaging in the future.

## Acknowledgments

We are grateful to all the participants in this study.

## Author contributions

Siqi Yang (Writing-original draft, Writing-review &amp; editing), Wei Liao (Resources, Software), Yimin Zhou (Formal analysis, Methodology), Chengzong Peng (Visualization), Juan Wang (Validation), and Zhi-qiang Zhang (Funding acquisition, Project administration).

## Supplementary material

Supplementary material is available at Cerebral Cortex online.

## Funding

This study was funded by the National Natural Science Foundation of China (82302293), the Science and Technology Foundation of Sichuan Province (2024NSFSC1782),and the Talent Introduction Research Projects of Chengdu University of Information Technology (KYTZ2023036).
