74:data from a multisite sample of 457 healthy individuals (47.3% female; aged 3 to 18 years) from the devCCNP. These data were used to construct the models, primarily based on the following considerations. First, while the original CentileBrain model encompasses a lifespan from 3 to 90 years, our study specifically focuses on the distribution of brain morphology during children's development (3 to 18 years). Secondly, although the original CentileBrain collected samples from diverse regions and ethnicities globally, our subsequent analysis of childhood epilepsy predominantly centered on the Chinese population. Leveraging the CentileBrain pipeline, we opted for multivariable fractional polynomial regression implemented with the mfp package in R. This algorithm can determine the functional form of the predictor by testing a wide family of shapes and multiple turning points while providing a good fit at the extremes of the covariates. The optimal covariate combination included site harmonization (ComBat-GAM) ( Pomponio et al. 2020) and the incorporation of intracranial volume, mean cortical thickness, and mean surface area in the regional models for subcortical volume, cortical thickness, and surface area regional measures, respectively.
